      "id": "5321d992bb1c7677c4baa7b926adc3cfdaeaf6c4",
      "message": "[ota-hal] OTA-1687: the mission layer remembers itself\n\nPunch items 6-8 of the contrary walker's list\n(docs/contrary-walker-bog-dragon-2026-09-05.md), the three that need no deed\nledger. Each was measured on the Bog Dragon by OTA-1686 and each flips a pin.\n\n6. ABANDON DROPS THE MISSION'S CONVERSATIONS. The walker abandoned the hunt at\n   stage 3 and took it again: the record restarted at stage 0, but the reeve's\n   and Old Mira's encounter records kept their `resolved` phase (keyed\n   family:id:stage) and the card component hides a resolved card - so the\n   re-accepted hunt showed no card at either person and only the typed verb\n   paid. abandonContract now forgets that mission's encounter records (hunt,\n   mystery, storyline - that mission's only); the next accept starts every\n   conversation fresh, and the reeve's card comes back.\n\n7. THE WRONG VERB ON THE RIGHT GROUND SAYS WHAT THE GROUND WANTS. Every\n   matcher spoke only when the verb matched and the ground did not (\"Not here\n   ... points elsewhere\"). \"negotiate\" and \"attack\" on the Cradle of Dusk - a\n   search stage, boots on the cell - drew nothing about the hunt. A stage verb\n   (investigate / diplomacy / attack / stealth / cast) that no tracked stage\n   pays, typed on a stage's own cell, out of combat, not naming a chip, now\n   draws: The Arbiter taps the slate. \"Not that. The Bog Dragon of Old Drakova\n   wants you to search this ground here.\" One reader,\n   missionTrace.stageUnderfoot, the same cell test as every other door.\n\n8. THE ESCORT CLEAR SAYS THE CLEAR, NOT THE NEXT BEAT. resolveStageEscortClear\n   printed nextDef.narration (and its Arbiter line) on the spot and carried\n   it on the close card: the walker read \"Mira reads the locket without\n   crying\" on the Mud Flood Nexus, 46 tiles from her holding, and \"the Dragon\n   uncoils from\" the steeple while standing on the Mud Seas - then read both\n   again on the ground, where advanceHunt and the card say them properly. When\n   the ground moves, the clear now prints \"The last of them is down.\" and the\n   \u25b8 Next direction on the feed and on the card, and the beat's prose prints\n   where the beat happens. A next stage on the SAME ground keeps the prose on\n   the spot (OTA-1622's same-tile close): no arrival will ever narrate it.\n\n- app/state/slices/questSlice.ts - forgetEncounters on abandon (three\n  families); the clear without the next narration.\n- app/engine/missionTrace.ts - stageUnderfoot.\n- app/state/gameStore.ts - the \"Not that\" line after the three matchers;\n  STAGE_VERB_INTENTS.\n- __tests__/ota1687TheMissionLayerRemembersItself.test.ts - 3 tests through\n  the store: the abandon forgets only that mission's records and the card\n  arms fresh; the line on the cell, nothing off it, nothing on \"look\"; the\n  brood cleared - clear + direction on feed and card, no apex prose - then the\n  apex prose on the steeple.\n- __tests__/ota1686TheContraryWalker.test.ts - two pins flipped.\n- __tests__/ota1578TheStageSaysWhoIsThere.test.ts,\n  __tests__/ota1630TheChipIsNotTheMission.test.ts - pins re-anchored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
      "dateCreated": "2026-09-05T08:10:20Z",
